  ('43b17333-a269-565c-9c3e-0feb5956811e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-sentence-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "While studying the migration data, ___." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Leilani's notes showed that the monarchs had left two weeks early","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"possessive-does-not-fix-dangling"},{"text":"the monarchs appeared to have left two weeks early","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"},{"text":"Leilani noticed that the monarchs had left two weeks early","is_correct":true},{"text":"it became clear that the monarchs had left two weeks early","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dangling-modifier"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Leilani noticed that the monarchs had left two weeks early$q$, $q$The person studying the data must be the subject after the opening phrase, and "Leilani" is that person. In the "Leilani's notes" choice the subject is "notes," so the notes seem to be studying the data; a possessive name does not fix the dangling modifier.$q$, 'draft', null)
