  ('ff6c5f48-0dee-50c5-80fe-9d11a8ef5f3b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-sentence-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The council's plan aims to widen the sidewalks, adding bike lanes, and that more trees will be planted along Main Street." Which revision corrects the faulty parallelism?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The council's plan aims to widen the sidewalks, add bike lanes, and plant more trees along Main Street.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The council's plan aims to widen the sidewalks, adding bike lanes, and planting more trees along Main Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism"},{"text":"The council's plan aims to widen the sidewalks, add bike lanes, and that more trees will be planted along Main Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism"},{"text":"The council's plan aims at widening the sidewalks, to add bike lanes, and planting more trees along Main Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"faulty-parallelism"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The council's plan aims to widen the sidewalks, add bike lanes, and plant more trees along Main Street.$q$, $q$All three goals now follow "to" as matching base verbs: "widen," "add," and "plant." The tempting choice that uses "adding" and "planting" still mixes those "-ing" forms with "to widen," so the list is not parallel.$q$, 'draft', null)
